# Install JAR into OneClient mods on each new version

Whenever this project ships a new `mod_version` (build, tag, or GitHub release of `farmhelper-fabric-*.jar`):

1. Run `./scripts/install-to-oneclient.sh` from the repo root (or the equivalent commands below).
2. Do this **after** `./gradlew build` (or `jar`) succeeds and the release JAR exists under `build/libs/`.
3. Confirm the mods folder contains exactly one FarmHelper JAR matching the new version.

## Target

```text
/home/geexy/.local/share/Polyfrost/OneClient/.minecraft/mods/26.3 Fabric/
```

## Required behavior

- Delete **only** previous FarmHelper artifacts in that folder:
  - `farmhelper-fabric-*.jar`
  - `FarmHelper*.jar` (legacy names, if any)
- Do **not** delete other mods or OneClient package symlinks.
- Copy the new release JAR (not `-sources.jar`, not `-dev.jar`) into that folder.
- Prefer the script: `./scripts/install-to-oneclient.sh [optional/path/to.jar]`

## Do not skip

Shipping a new `26.3.0-clean.N` (or any later version) without updating this mods folder is incomplete work for this project.
